From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:43:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 64/79] runner: Flash-Next acts in thinking chats only, inside
 the think block

The in-model runner is in-thinking only. A runner binding's family may now default the scan spans to
`reasoning` (PREFIX_SPANS still overrides; `all` keeps every span). Flash-Next's binding does; DeepSeek-V4.1's keeps
every span, so its default is unchanged. With the spans `reasoning`, server/chat.zig opens no runner session for a
non-thinking chat (no cells closed or run, no owned value, no runner guide), so its bytes are the runner-off server's.
Before, a non-thinking reply closed cells speculatively and could own an inline value in the answer (TP2 miabench: 30
non-thinking replies closed 75 cells, one owned; TP1 thinking-off set: tc-comp-09 owned one).

Tests: through openai.run, a non-thinking chat gets no session, 0 cells and the runner-off server's bytes; a thinking
chat keeps its session and owns only in the think block. Flash-Next's binding defaults to the think block, and a
thinking reply's answer triggers nothing.

(cherry picked from commit 1a7ed13bb4fac1cc440efd716655e35570bc134d)
